ed seats in the country, and first-term Republican Gabe Evans is defending it against Democrat Manny Rutinel in a midterm climate that favors the out party. Ten expert ratings split between calling the race a tossup and a Democratic-leaning flip, and prediction markets price Rutinel as a clear favorite, with two platforms near 85 percent and a third at 75.\n\nMoney tells a mixed story: Evans holds a large cash-on-hand lead, but Rutinel has raised heavily and benefits from roughly $3.5 million in supportive outside spending, several times what Evans has drawn. The only public poll, from a Republican-leaning firm in mid-September, showed Evans ahead by two. The race sits as a Democratic lean heading into Election Day, with Evans' incumbency and the district's even balance keeping it competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6862, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7621, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7968, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7638, "margin": 4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8011, "margin": 4.6}]}